- Add: FDA `schema` is now re-derived from the materialized Parquet after every successful fetch, so it reports the actual DuckDB types of the stored data and stays up to date when the source data shape changes over time (#235)
- Add: MongoDB FDAs no longer report a `VARCHAR` placeholder before their first fetch; their columns are persisted with `"type": null` until the actual types can be derived from the materialized Parquet (#235)
- Add: cached MongoDB FDAs created in `strict` mode must now declare their output columns (`projection`, or a final `$project`/`$group` aggregation stage). The column set is no longer inferred from a single sampled document, which could silently omit fields missing from that sample (#235)
- Add: sliding-window (partitioned) refresh support for MongoDB FDAs, for both `filter` and `aggregation` queries, mirroring the existing PostgreSQL window refresh policy (#194)
- Fix: deleting an FDA while it is being fetched (including its initial fetch) is now rejected with `409 FDAProcessing`; deletion atomically moves the FDA to a new `deleting` status (#220)
- Fix: the `error` of a failed FDA refresh is now cleared once a later refresh completes, instead of being reported alongside `status: completed` (#321)
- Fix: preserve numeric precision and consistent types across cached and fresh responses; large integers are returned as exact JSON numbers, cached DECIMAL values as strings, and large Number DA parameters are bound as exact integers (#291)
- Fix: cron refresh intervals are now measured deterministically in UTC over a full cycle, so a valid combination such as a monthly cron with a `month` partition is no longer rejected depending on the date the FDA is created or on daylight saving changes (#316)
- Fix: `clean-partition` now removes the partitions that fall outside `windowSize`; it was looking under `<fdaId>/` instead of `<fdaId>.parquet/`, so no partition was ever deleted (#323)
- Fix: object storage listings are now paginated and deletions batched, so FDAs with more than 1000 objects are fully removed on `DELETE` and fully considered by `clean-partition` (#323)
- Fix: deleting an FDA also removes its leftover staging objects under `tmp/` (#323)
- Fix: FDA upload flow now marks status as `completed` only after `defaultDataAccess` is created (#308)
- Fix: MongoDB FDA aggregation pipelines are now validated against an allowlist of read-only stages instead of a blacklist of write stages. Cross-collection stages (`$lookup`, `$graphLookup`, `$unionWith`, `$documents`) and administrative/introspection stages (e.g. `$indexStats`, `$currentOp`) are no longer permitted, including when nested inside a `$facet` sub-pipeline. Existing FDAs using a now-disallowed stage will fail on their next refresh/query execution (#286)
- Fix: `strict` PostgreSQL FDAs now detect changes in the columns of their source query (added, removed, renamed, reordered or retyped) on every refresh and adopt them with a full rebuild of the FDA, instead of failing on every refresh or silently storing data under the old column names (#181)
- Fix: `PUT /{visibility}/fdas/{fdaId}` validates the source query of `strict` PostgreSQL FDAs before regenerating them and returns `400 InvalidParam` if it is no longer valid (#181)
- Fix: partitioned FDAs are read with DuckDB `union_by_name`, so partitions written with different columns or types (e.g. after a source schema change in `unchecked` FDAs, or MongoDB windows with sparse fields) can be queried together, filling missing columns with `NULL` (#181)
- Update: @duckdb/node-api dependency version from 1.5.5-r.4 to 1.5.6-r1
- Replace MinIO docker image by PGsty image (#302)
